.TH SISTA-ANSI 3 "2026-10-04" "Sista 3.0.3"
.SH NAME
sista-ansi \- configure terminal colors and text attributes
.SH LIBRARY
Sista C++ library (libSista, \fI-lSista\fP)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sista/ansi.hpp>

.B "void sista::setForegroundColor(ForegroundColor color);"
.B "void sista::setBackgroundColor(BackgroundColor color);"
.B "void sista::setAttribute(Attribute attribute);"
.B "void sista::resetAttribute(Attribute attribute);"
.B "void sista::resetAnsi();"
.B "struct sista::RGBColor;"
.B "struct sista::ANSISettings;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The free functions write ANSI control sequences to standard output.
Overloads accept named colors, RGB values, or 256-color palette indexes.
.PP
.B ANSISettings
stores foreground and background colors plus one or more attributes.
.B apply()
writes the stored settings;
.B reset()
resets those settings.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The setters and reset functions return no value.
The corresponding string helpers return the control sequence without
writing it.
.SH NOTES
Terminal capabilities vary, particularly for RGB colors and uncommon
attributes.
Reset changed settings before returning control to the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <iostream>
#include <sista/sista.hpp>

int main()
{
    sista::setForegroundColor(sista::ForegroundColor::GREEN);
    std::cout << "ready";
    sista::resetAnsi();
    std::cout << '\en';
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sista-border (3),
.BR sista-cursor (3),
.BR sista-pawn (3),
.BR sista (7)
